# Phase 3 remoting transport review — 2026-09-27 (continued)

- Scope: Java 5.5.1 parity correction for per-connection outbound queue and matching English/Traditional Chinese plan language; Phase 3 only.
- Changed the connection outbound path from bounded Tokio MPSC with capacity waits/rejection to an unbounded FIFO. Enqueue is immediate; active write/send completion retains operation deadline and connection shutdown discards remaining backlog. Removed production queue-capacity state and queue-full error. Semaphore admission and other bounded queues remain unchanged.
- Matched Netty 4.1 default write watermarks (64 KiB high / 32 KiB low) when Rust explicit high/low values are not both positive; custom values remain applied only as a pair. Updated `is_channel_writable` documentation and compatibility ledger to describe watermark status, not queue capacity.
- Updated the saturation unit/loopback tests to show enqueue beyond the former 128 frames while peer reads are withheld, retain blocked active-write deadline verification, and renamed the inbound-response test to describe an unbounded backlog. Updated both Phase 3 plan files per the user's explicit instruction that Java behavior takes precedence over prior bounded-queue plan language. Updated compatibility docs and ADR.
- Initial full-suite Clippy found a `map_or` simplification in the new connection path; fixed it. Follow-up audit found the optional watermark representation no longer meaningful after adopting defaults, so watermarks are now a concrete tuple and configurations with either threshold unset use Java defaults.
- Validation passed: `cargo fmt --all --check`; `cargo test --workspace --offline` (common 11, protocol 9 + 1 fixture, remoting 41 unit + 4 codec + 72 transport); `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --offline -- -D warnings`; `python3 scripts/check-workspace-metadata.py`; `python3 tests/differential/compare.py --self-test`; `git diff --check`.
- Queue change, matching plan updates and documentation are currently uncommitted; no commit created in this session yet. Phase 3 remains unaccepted; no Phase 4 work started. Remaining parity/API/oneway/lifecycle and test-evidence blockers from the previous log remain open.
